  "summary": "Selected evidence records: sandboxd is an open-source, self-hosted AI app builder: a prompt causes a coding agent to build a real app in an isolated sandbox on the user's server, each app live at a preview URL. The system is a single Go control-plane binary that shells out to the Docker CLI (no SDK), fronted by Traefik for preview routing, with SQLite (WAL) as the source of truth and an in-sandbox supervisor called runtimed baked into the base image.",
